{{!--
    reference/params - one parameter group (path, query or header) for an operation.
    Renders nothing when the group is empty, so callers can include all three
    unconditionally.
    Params:
      title  - group heading, e.g. "Query parameters" (required)
      params - array of parameter view models from lib/api-reference/model.js (required)
      flags  - parameter names, when the model recognised the group as a flag list rather
               than N documented parameters (optional; see flagNames() in model.js)

    Rows are reference/schema-node: buildParameter() emits the same field names as a
    schema tree node, so a parameter renders identically to a property without a
    second copy of the row markup.

    A flag list is the exception. GET /v1/settings takes 87 same-typed, undocumented
    booleans that together answer one question - which settings do you want back - and a
    row each made roughly 260 lines of page carrying no more information than the chip
    grid below. The model only sets `flags` when every member of the group is uniform, so
    nothing with a description or a required member can land here.
--}}
{{#if params.length}}
<div class="mt-4">
    {{> reference/section-heading label=title class="mb-2"}}
    {{#if flags}}
    <p class="text-base-content/70 mb-2 text-sm">Set any of these to <code class="ee-chip">true</code> to include it in the
        response. All default to <code class="ee-chip">false</code>.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1">
        {{#each flags}}<code class="ee-chip">{{this}}</code>{{/each}}
    </div>
    {{else}}
    <ul class="ee-ref-props">
        {{#each params}}{{> reference/schema-node}}{{/each}}
    </ul>
    {{/if}}
</div>
{{/if}}
